  "query_preview": "(Today through Friday)...\nIssued at 1233 AM EST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\nAnother 24 to 36 hours of warm and dry weather is expected before a \ncold front brings an abrupt shift to end the weekend and start the \ncoming Thanksgiving week.\n\nHigh pressure will remain in control today, and we continue to \noutpace blend numbers on highs. Expect upper 60s to low 70s across \nthe area today, with plentiful sunshine yet again.\n\nGuidance continues to slow the front, as it has been doing for \nseveral days - not unusual when dealing with entrenched high \npressure - and this has delayed the arrival of rain to mainly Sunday \nafternoon into Sunday night. Expectations remain just showers, with \nlittle to no instability to speak of. Precipitable water values will \napproach climatological max, but in a fairly narrow axis along the \nfront. A brief heavy downpour is certainly not out of the question \nbut this will not be enough to have significant impact, particularly \ngiven the dry antecedent conditions.\n\nNext week will bring an abrupt Thanksgiving about face in the wake \nof the cold front, bringing temperatures back down to near to \nslightly below normal, with widespread highs in the 40s and lows \nwell into the 20s on some nights.\n\nGuidance is coming into better agreement on the handling of a couple \nof closed upper lows mid to late week - likely to increase cloud \ncover and perhaps produce some light precip in the area, though the \nfar more significant impacts of this system appear to be in store \nfor the east coast and New England.",
